    <fr:title text="Chain Rule of Mutual Info">Chain Rule of Mutual Info</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>Theorem</fr:taxon>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter><html:p>
    We have that
<fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
      \begin {align*}
        I(X, Y; Z) = I(X; Z) + I(Y; Z | X)
      \end {align*}
    ]]></fr:tex></html:p>
  
  
 <html:div class="jms-callout" style="
  margin: 1.1rem 0;
  padding: 0.1rem 0 0.1rem 0.9rem;
  border-left: 2px solid rgb(109, 103, 101);
  "><html:span style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(109, 103, 101);" /> 
  <html:details><html:summary><html:span class="foldout" style="font-weight: 500; color: rgb(109, 103, 101);">Proof.</html:span></html:summary>
    By definition,
    <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
        \begin {align*}
          I(X, Y; Z) &= H(X,Y) + H(Z) - H(X, Y, Z) \\
          &= H(X) + H(Y | X) + H(Z) - H(X, Z) - H(Y | X, Z) \\
          &= H(X) + H(Y | X) + H(Z) - H(X, Z) - H(Y | X, Z) \\
          &= I(X; Z) + H(Y | X) - (H(Y, Z | X) - H(Z | X)) \\
          &= I(X; Z) + I(Y; Z | X)
        \end {align*}
    ]]></fr:tex>
    as desired
  </html:details>
</html:div>


